 ALTERNATIVES: an "Open app" button in the task detail as the component specification draws it, rejected because a preview runs the whole job's project and the detail belongs to one task, which the assumption log records; a new tab of the evidence panel, rejected for the same reason, because that panel shows one task run; rewriting README images on the server, rejected because the server would have to write the caller's token into the fragment; parsing the fragment in the browser, rejected because the cockpit's tests have no DOM and the server's output has one fixed image shape; polling while the panel is closed, rejected because the idle stop exists for a preview nobody is looking at.
 
 HOW TO REVERSE: delete `apps/ui/src/api/artifactPreview.ts`, `apps/ui/src/api/previewSend.ts`, the directory `apps/ui/src/components/artifacts/`, their tests, `tests/ui_contracts/test_artifact_preview.py`, the two doors in `remedyApi.ts`, the button in `RightLivePanel.tsx`, the state and the mount in `RemedyShell.tsx`, the assumption log's F041 line and this paragraph.
+
+## DECISION F041 D6 — the guided tour gains a `preview` anchor, offered as a "See it running" stop only when the job's own project folder resolves a runtime, whose "Show me" opens the Results panel; and the preview flow is proved end to end by one subprocess test that drives a real UI server and a real small app from start to the idle stop (2026-09-29)
+
+CONTEXT: T5_F041.md asks that the tour's stops can target the preview, and T5_F036.md reserves exactly that ("Enhanced by: F041 preview links from tour stops"); its acceptance asks for an end-to-end run on a fixture app, open, a live link that works, idle, stopped, and the state truthful, with no process left. Measured by the reviewer at `fd124cc9`: `TOUR_ANCHOR_KINDS` in `packages/orchestration/result_tour.py` is `("node", "diff", "evidence", "command")`, mirrored in order by `apps/ui/src/api/resultTour.ts` and pinned by `tests/ui_contracts/test_tour_view_contract.py`, by a literal in `tests/orchestration/test_result_tour.py` and by `resultTour.test.ts`; `anchor_problem` refuses every other kind; `fallback_tour_stops` builds how it ended, the changed areas, how to run it and the Definition of Done within `MAX_TOUR_STOPS`, eight; `build_tour_prompt` lists one allowed anchor per line; the tour tests build their jobs with an empty `repo_path`, and `Path("").resolve()` is the working directory, which in this checkout resolves the cockpit's own vite runtime; `resolve_spec` in `packages/runtimes/runtime_config.py` reads a folder's configuration and detection files and runs nothing, and its module imports `dev_server`, which imports `subprocess`; `RemedyShell.tsx`'s `handleTourShowAnchor` acts on node and diff only; the UI server's preview worker reads `preview.idle_ttl_seconds` once when the server starts and steps at least every fifteen seconds; and `tests/runtimes/test_runtime_cli_process_boundary.py` already runs a stdlib app under a `[runtime]` configuration at a port from `tests/ports.py`, marked `subprocess`.
+
+CHOSEN: (1) THE ANCHOR: `preview` joins `TOUR_ANCHOR_KINDS` last, in both languages, with the one ref `app`; it resolves only when the job is previewable, which is true exactly when its `repo_path` is a non-empty string naming a directory and `resolve_spec` accepts it, imported inside the function that asks. (2) THE STOP: a previewable job's mechanical tour gains "See it running", after "How to run it" and before the Definition of Done, and the room for changed areas shrinks by one, so the ceiling of eight holds; the model's prompt lists `preview app` among its anchors only for such a job, and every other tour and prompt stays byte for byte as it is. (3) THE CLIENT: the label is "The app preview", "Show me" is offered for it, and the shell opens the Results panel for it. (4) THE PROOF: `tests/ui_server/test_preview_end_to_end.py` saves a job whose project is a stdlib app configured by `.remedy/config.toml`, starts a real UI server in a thread with an idle limit of two seconds, sends the start through the write door, reads the view until it is live and finds no link before that, fetches the link, then stops reading and waits on the record on disk until the server's own worker has stopped the preview for want of a viewer, and holds that the view says so, that the link no longer answers and that the app's and the supervisor's processes are gone. (5) R-1106 is repaired in the same round.
+
+ALTERNATIVES: a preview stop on every tour, rejected because a project with nothing to run would be sent to a card that says so; asking the preview record whether a preview ever ran, rejected because the tour is built when the job ends, before anybody has started one; an end-to-end test at the worker alone with a fake clock, rejected because the acceptance names the command's path through the door and a fake clock would not show that the server's own worker stops a preview nobody views; waiting for the idle stop by reading the view, rejected because each read of the view counts as a viewer and would keep the preview alive.
+
+HOW TO REVERSE: remove `preview` from both anchor lists and their tests, the `previewable` field, `_project_previewable`, the preview stop, its prompt line and its branch in `anchor_problem`, the shell's branch in `handleTourShowAnchor`, the label and `tourCanShow` case, delete `tests/ui_server/test_preview_end_to_end.py`, and delete this paragraph.
