+- R-1106 — Low, THE README REWRITE SHIELDS ITS OWN IMAGE TAGS WITH A TEXT MARKER, SO A README THAT SPELLS THE MARKER GETS AN IMAGE OR THE WORD `undefined` IN ITS PLACE. Raised by the planner and reviewer of F041's second session at the round 5 gate. SEARCHED BEFORE MINTING (checklist item 30): the open set at `fd124cc9` is empty, and neither the ledger nor its archive names `readmeCockpitHtml` or its marker. MEASURED at `fd124cc9`: `readmeCockpitHtml` in `apps/ui/src/api/artifactPreview.ts` replaces each recognised capture image with the text `@@artifact-image-<n>@@`, removes every other image tag, and then replaces every such marker in the whole fragment with the tag stored at that index; the server's renderer passes that text through from a README unchanged, so a README holding `@@artifact-image-0@@` and no image renders `undefined`, and one holding it beside a capture image renders the capture twice. The reviewer's own vitest probe in a disposable worktree read both. The marker was the worker's answer to the block's own order to run the removal pass after the rewrite, which as written would also have removed the tags just built. WHY LOW: nothing the server did not sanitize reaches the page, because a marker can only become a tag this function built itself or the word `undefined`, but the README is shown wrong and the code's own comment says a README cannot spell the marker. FIX: one replacement over the alternation of the recognised shape and any other image tag, so a rewritten tag is never read again and no marker exists, under a comment naming this finding, and tests that a README spelling the marker, with no image and beside a capture image, comes back with that text unchanged. Owner: F041.
